  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 1248 PM MST Mon Nov 2 2026\n\nWeak upper wave sneaks through the central Rockies late Wed into\nThu morning, bringing widespread but generally light showers to\nmany locations, heaviest Wed night. Precip amounts will be under\na quarter inch, but with snow levels falling toward 7000 feet \nby Thu morning, higher terrain locations could see a quick inch \nor two of snow before precip ends. Generally dry/mild weather \nthen returns from Thu afternoon into Fri, before another weak \nwave brings back a few mountains showers Fri night/Sat morning. \nWeekend now looks dry and warmer as swrn upper ridge builds and \nmain trough axis shifts eastward into the Great Lakes.",
